/-!
# The group `semiLin K` is solvable

This file proves `Work.Hering.AppVIII.semiLin_solvable`: the group `semiLin K` of maps
`(x,y) ↦ (a₁ · Φ^i x, η x + a₂ · Φ^i y)` (with `Φ = x ↦ x ^ 2` the Frobenius automorphism of
the finite field `K` of characteristic two) is solvable.

The argument is the following.  Write `Γ ≤ Equiv.Perm K` for the group of semilinear maps
`x ↦ a · Φ^i x` of `K`.  An element `f ∈ semiLin K` is determined by how it acts on
`K × {0}` and on `{0} × K` up to an additive constant: the two maps

* `semiFirst f : x ↦ (f (x,0)).1`, and
* `semiSecond f : y ↦ (f (0,y)).2 - (f (0,0)).2`

are semilinear, and `semiPsi f = (semiFirst f, semiSecond f)` defines a group homomorphism
`semiLin K →* Γ × Γ` whose kernel is exactly the group `S ≤ semiLin K` of shear maps
`(x,y) ↦ (x, η x + y)`.

`S` is abelian, and `Γ` is solvable: the scalars `Λ = {x ↦ a x} ◁ Γ` form an abelian group with
`Γ / Λ` cyclic (generated by the class of `Φ`), so that `Γ` is an extension of an abelian group
by an abelian group.  Hence `Γ × Γ` is solvable, and `semiLin K` is solvable as an extension of
the abelian group `S` by `Γ × Γ` (`Group.isSolvable_of_ker_le_range`).

All auxiliary definitions and lemmas are in `Submission.Work.Hering.AppVIII.SemiLinAux`.
-/

namespace Work.Hering.AppVIII

theorem semiLin_solvable (K : Type*) [Field K] [CharP K 2] [Finite K] :
    Group.IsSolvable (semiLin K) := by
  haveI := shearSub_isSolvable K
  exact Group.isSolvable_of_ker_le_range (shearSub K).subtype (semiPsi K)
    (by
      rw [Subgroup.range_subtype]
      exact semiPsi_ker_le_shearSub K)

end Work.Hering.AppVIII
